# CockroachDB

Enforcement: **B**. Not interchangeable with single-node PostgreSQL despite wire compatibility myths.

## Distinctives

- Data distributed by primary key / column families — design keys for locality.
- Multi-row transactions that span ranges cost more; minimize.
- Prefer UUID/unordered keys carefully — watch hot ranges from monotonic keys.
- Online schema changes have stages; follow CRDB migration guidance.
- Follower reads / exact staleness are explicit choices — document consistency needs.
- `SERIAL`/`SEQUENCE`-like patterns can create hotspots — prefer alternatives recommended for CRDB.

## Do not

- Assume every PostgreSQL extension or feature exists
- Ignore range hotspots under load tests
